<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <RootNamespace>Databento.CSharpApiClient</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Databento.CSharpApiClient</AssemblyName>
    <Nullable>disable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>disable</ImplicitUsings>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1734</NoWarn>
    <WarningsAsErrors>$(WarningsAsErrors);CS1591</WarningsAsErrors>

    <!-- Debug symbols + Source Link: ship a .snupkg so consumers can step into the source. -->
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <DebugType>portable</DebugType>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <Deterministic>true</Deterministic>
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(CI)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>

    <!-- NuGet packaging -->
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <PackageId>Databento.CSharpApiClient</PackageId>
    <Version>2.8.0</Version>
    <Authors>Vardan Tovmasyan</Authors>
    <Description>Pure-managed C# HTTP client for the Databento Historical API. Covers timeseries (DBN binary and JSON), metadata, batch jobs, and symbology. No native dependencies — works on any .NET 8+ runtime.</Description>
    <PackageTags>databento;market-data;trading;options;equities;historical;api-client;dbn</PackageTags>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/mrut2pac/Databento.CSharpApiClient</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/mrut2pac/Databento.CSharpApiClient</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
v2.8.0 - 2026-11-26

Changed
- DatabentoJsonClient: a time-series request whose end is after the dataset's available end now throws
  DatabentoHttpException (422, Code DataEndAfterAvailableEnd), as DatabentoClient always has, instead of returning no
  records. Code that relied on the empty answer must catch the exception or end the range at the available end.

Fixed
- The README's link to the CHANGELOG works on the nuget.org package page.

v2.7.2 - 2026-11-26

Fixed
- JsonRecordReader, and the JSON client's responses, read a JSON array document one record at a time as it arrives,
  instead of reading the whole document into strings first, which held a large array several times over on the
  large object heap. An array is still recognized by a leading [ (after a UTF-8 byte order mark); an array in UTF-16
  or UTF-32 no longer is.

v2.7.1 - 2026-11-25

Added
- StatTypes: the stat_type values of the statistics schema (OpenInterest, SettlementPrice, ...), to compare
  IStatisticsRecord.StatType with instead of a bare number.
- Datasets: the 18 current datasets it lacked, among them DbixCore (DBIX.CORE), EqusMini, XnasBasic, XnysPillar,
  IfusImpact and XeurEobi.
- DatabentoErrorCase.DatasetUnavailableRange: the dataset_unavailable_range error case, which Databento answers for
  a range outside what the dataset makes available to the API key. It mapped to Unknown before.

v2.7.0 - 2026-11-24

Added
- IDatabentoTimeseriesClient: the CBBO, BBO, TCBBO, trades, OHLCV and statistics calls, returning the record
  interfaces, so code can take either client or another implementation, such as a cache, or a fake in tests.
  It holds the 11 async calls for several symbols; DatabentoTimeseriesClientExtensions adds the one-symbol and
  sync forms. Both clients implement it explicitly, so their own methods are unchanged. Each call returns a new
  array the caller owns, and a call added later comes with a default implementation that throws
  NotSupportedException.

v2.6.0 — 2026-11-24

Changed
- The requests that carry a symbol list send their parameters as a POST form, as Databento's own client does: the
  timeseries calls of DatabentoJsonClient and DatabentoClient, and GetCostAsync, GetRecordCountAsync and
  GetBillableSizeAsync, with their sync forms. So one request can carry the 2,000 symbols the API takes; in a GET
  query string fewer than 300 OPRA symbols already passed the 8 KB a server accepts. Parameters and answers are
  the same, and a 429 or 5xx answer is retried as before.
- Compatibility: the parameters are no longer in the URI. A custom IHttpTransport, mock or cache that tells these
  requests apart by URI must read the form body; a GET-only retry policy or cache no longer acts on them; and a
  BaseUri that redirects with 301/302 loses the form, as a redirected POST is resent as a GET.

v2.5.0 — 2026-11-23

Added
- DbnToJsonExtensions.ToJsonRecord(): returns a BBO, CBBO, TCBBO, trade, OHLCV or statistics DBN record as its
  JSON model, with the values DatabentoJsonClient reads from the JSON encoding of the same record, so records
  downloaded as DBN can be saved as JSON and read back like records downloaded as JSON. A value the JSON model
  can't hold (a CBBO size, or a CBBO or TCBBO bid or ask size, beyond int.MaxValue, or an OHLCV volume beyond
  long.MaxValue) throws OverflowException.
- Batch split options: SubmitBatchJobAsync/SubmitBatchJob take a BatchJobRequest with SplitDuration, SplitSymbols
  and SplitSize. Its encoding, compression and split duration are the enums BatchEncoding, BatchCompression and
  BatchSplitDuration; a split option left unset is left to the API (one file per day). The positional overloads
  send what they sent before.
- JsonRecordReader: reads the records of JSON data the caller already has (such as a downloaded batch file), as
  DbnReader does for DBN, with or without pretty prices and timestamps (batch jobs leave them off by default).
  A line that doesn't parse, JSON that is no record, or a record of another schema throws InvalidDataException.
- BatchJobStates: constants for the batch job states.

Changed
- DatabentoJsonClient: a response read whole as a JSON array that doesn't parse throws DatabentoException, as a
  line that doesn't parse does (it threw JsonException).

Deprecated
- SymbolTypes.Nasdaq, OccSymbol, Cfi and Isin: the Historical API refuses them with HTTP 400; it takes only
  raw_symbol, parent, instrument_id and continuous.

Fixed
- CbboRecordJson.Price and BboRecordJson.Price read a price written without pretty prices (an integer of 1e-9)
  scaled, as every other price is; they read it unscaled.

v2.4.0 — 2026-11-18

Added
- Stream*Async (async enumerable) and Stream* (sync enumerable) beside every timeseries Get*Async that is
  not obsolete, on both clients. Records are yielded as they are decoded, so a large request no longer has to
  fit in memory. Only the HTTP status (429 and 5xx) is retried, before the body is read; a failure mid-body
  is thrown, never retried. Each enumeration sends a new request.
- DbnReader: streams the records of DBN data the caller already has (such as a downloaded batch file) from any
  Stream, async and sync. Zstandard-compressed data has to be decompressed by the caller.

Changed
- Every Get*Async collects the matching stream instead of reading the whole body into memory first; its
  records are unchanged.
- DatabentoClient: a connection that drops while the body is read throws the IOException the response stream
  raises (it threw HttpRequestException; DatabentoJsonClient already threw the IOException).
- Cut-short or malformed DBN data fails with InvalidDataException (it threw EndOfStreamException, or a record
  cut inside its header ended the data quietly). Check code that catches the old exception types.

Fixed
- DBN v1 data (served for e.g. XNAS.ITCH and OPRA.PILLAR): records had Symbol always null and DbnMetadata was
  misread after Limit. The v1 layout is now read. DbnMetadata.FromBinaryReader also refuses leftover non-zero
  metadata bytes and DBN versions other than 1 to 3, with InvalidDataException.

v2.3.0 — 2026-11-17

Added
- Record interfaces that the JSON and DBN record classes both implement: IRecord, IBboRecord, ICbboRecord,
  ITcbboRecord, ITradeRecord, IOhlcvRecord and IStatisticsRecord. Flat like DBN, DBN types where the two
  differ, and an undefined price, quantity or timestamp reads as null.
- Symbol on the bbo, cbbo, tcbbo, trades, ohlcv and statistics DBN records, from the stream's symbol mappings.
  For DBN client users, each decoded record holds one more reference (8 bytes on 64-bit, about 7-10% of a record); the symbol
  string itself is shared by every record of that symbol.

Changed
- DatabentoJsonClient: records of a single-symbol request carry that symbol in Symbol (it was null).

v2.2.0 — 2026-10-07

Added
- DefinitionRecordDbn decodes every field of both DBN layouts (it read 19), with the same properties as
  DefinitionRecordJson.
- ImbalanceRecordDbn.AuctionTime (null when undefined), OrderBookAction.Cancel / None,
  ListBatchJobs(states, since), BatchFile.Urls, and the BatchJob fields the API sends.

Fixed
- DBN decoders: MBO read the channel as Action and the action as Side; tcbbo / cmbp-1 AskPublisherId
  was always 0; cbbo-1s / cbbo-1m read the book level 8 bytes early.
- BatchJob.JobId was always null (the API sends id); BatchJob.Symbols failed to read the comma-joined
  string the API sends; BatchFile.HttpsUrl / FtpUrl were always null; ListBatchJobs ignored its filters.
- DefinitionRecordJson.ContractMultiplier read its undefined value as 2147483647; it now reads NaN.

Deprecated (to be removed in the next major version)
- ListBatchJobs(dataset, state), BatchJob.Files and ImbalanceRecordDbn.AuctionTimeUtc.

v2.1.0 — 2026-10-07

Added
- DefinitionRecordJson: the 54 fields the API sends that weren't mapped (currencies, lot and trade-size
  limits, maturity parts, UnderlyingId, RawInstrumentId, the DBN v3 Leg* fields, and more).
- ImbalanceRecordJson.AuctionTime, DateRange.Schemas (SchemaRange), SymbologyResolution.Message / Status,
  UnitPriceInfo.UnitPrices and DatasetCondition.Date.

Fixed
- GetDatasetCondition with a date returned the dataset's first day; it now returns the requested day
  (null for a day without an entry), and the most recent day when no date is given.
- ListConditions always failed with 404; it now calls metadata.get_dataset_condition.

Deprecated (to be removed in the next major version)
- GetSymbolMappings (no symbol_mapping schema; use ResolveSymbols) and GetOhlcvEod (no dataset serves
  ohlcv-eod; use GetOhlcv1d).
- Properties the API never sends: UnitPriceInfo.UnitPrice, DatasetCondition.DateGenerated,
  PublisherInfo.Name, FieldInfo.Description, and TsInDelta / Depth / Sequence on the BBO, tcbbo and
  cmbp-1 records (JSON and DBN).

v2.0.1 — 2026-10-07

Fixed
- ResolveSymbols returned every interval with Symbol, StartDate and EndDate null: the API sends
  them as s, d0 and d1. EndDate is the exclusive end of the interval.

v2.0.0 — 2026-10-06

Breaking (public property types, required by the fixes below)
- StatisticsRecordJson.Quantity and StatisticsRecordDbn.Quantity: int -> long.
- StatusRecordJson.Action, Reason and TradingEvent: string -> ushort, matching StatusRecordDbn.

Fixed
- ResolveSymbols resolved only the last symbol of a multi-symbol request: symbols now travel in
  one comma-joined field, as symbology.resolve keeps only the last of repeated fields.
- Statistics (JSON) threw on any 64-bit quantity, including INT64_MAX for "no quantity".
- Statistics (DBN) misread every field after price on DBN v3 data (80-byte records); both the
  v3 and the older layout are now decoded, chosen by record length.
- Status (JSON) threw on every record: action, reason and trading_event are numeric codes.
- Definitions (DBN) misread the strike and instrument class in DBN v1 (360-byte records) and
  almost every field in DBN v3 (520-byte records); both layouts are now decoded, verified
  against live records, and any other length is refused instead of misread.
- DefinitionRecordJson.Action was always null: the API names the field security_update_action.
- Undefined DBN timestamps (u64::MAX) now decode as null rather than a bogus date.

v1.4.0 — 2026-09-17

Added
- DatabentoOptions.RequestCompressedResponses (default true) to turn response compression off.

Changed
- Requests now negotiate a compressed response: the client sends Accept-Encoding and the runtime
  decodes the Content-Encoding the API answers with, transparently, before the body reaches the
  caller. Market data is highly repetitive, so a timeseries response is substantially smaller on
  the wire - one session of option CBBO measured 117 KB uncompressed against 8.1 KB gzipped.
- DownloadBatchFileAsync is exempt and negotiates nothing, so a stored artifact is delivered
  exactly as stored rather than being decoded in flight.

v1.3.0 — 2026-09-17

Added
- JSON records returned by timeseries.get_range now expose the raw Symbol they belong to,
  populated from the API's map_symbols field. Covers every timeseries schema: bbo, cbbo,
  cmbp-1, definition, imbalance, mbo, mbp-1, mbp-10, ohlcv, statistics, status, tbbo,
  tcbbo and trades.

Changed
- A timeseries request covering more than one symbol (or ALL_SYMBOLS) now sends
  map_symbols=true, so an interleaved response can be split per symbol without a second
  symbology call. A single-symbol request is unchanged and does not send it: the caller
  already knows the symbol and the field is repeated on every record.

v1.2.2 — 2026-06-15

Fixed
- JSON client returned zero records for responses whose numeric fields are string-encoded
  (pretty_px=true, e.g. "price":"4.000000000"): such values now read into the numeric DTO
  properties via JsonNumberHandling.AllowReadingFromString.
- A record that fails to deserialize now throws DatabentoException instead of being silently
  dropped, so a parse failure can no longer masquerade as an empty result.

Added
- Symbol package (.snupkg) + Source Link for step-into debugging.

v1.2.1 — 2026-06-13 (docs/metadata update; no API changes)
See v1.2.0 below for the full feature release.

v1.2.0 — 2026-06-13

Added
- DatabentoJsonClient: full Historical API JSON coverage — new schemas: mbo, mbp-10,
  bbo-1s, bbo-1m, tbbo, tcbbo, cmbp-1, status, imbalance, symbol_mapping; new metadata
  endpoints: list_conditions, get_record_count, get_billable_size, get_cost.
- DatabentoClient (DBN binary): full schema coverage — MboRecordDbn, Mbp10RecordDbn,
  TbboRecordDbn, TcbboRecordDbn, Cmbp1RecordDbn, BboRecordDbn, StatusRecordDbn,
  ImbalanceRecordDbn, StatisticsRecordDbn, DefinitionRecordDbn, SymbolMappingRecordDbn.
- Adaptive MBO body layout: handles DBN v1 (40-byte, no channel_id) and v2 (48-byte).

Fixed
- TBBO decoder now accepts rtype 0x01 (Mbp1) as sent by the live Databento API.

Full history: https://github.com/mrut2pac/Databento.CSharpApiClient/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" Condition="Exists('..\..\README.md')" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.SourceLink.GitHub" Version="8.0.0" PrivateAssets="all" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
